<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Norilsk says some metal for export seized.</title>
<headline>Russia's Norilsk says some metal for export seized.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Norilsk Nickel said on Tuesday that the tax police had seized 625 billion roubles' worth of metals intended for export but that other tonnages were being exported according to schedule.</p>
<p>Yuri Oleinikov and Sergei Vetchinin, spokesmen for RAO Norilsky Nikel, declined to name the volumes or types of metal confiscated, which Oleinikov put at half a cargo's worth, but said other output was being exported according to plan.</p>
</text>
